    "description": "Full-spectrum audit of Huang, Choi, McClean &amp; Preskill (2025) \"The vast world of quantum advantage\" (arXiv:2508.05720). This paper subjects both the Huang et al. five-keystone framework and QNFO's own prior critiques to symmetric scrutiny. Key findings: Theorem 1 is the most sophisticated challenge to QNFO's epistemic posture yet produced; QNFO has five documented vulnerabilities including the \"Shor's Assumptions\" gap; maximum convergence on core values but irreducible uncertainty on implications. Includes a 9-stage Bayesian cascade analysis, a 12-entry calibration register (2027-2035), and a diversified portfolio recommendation.",
